# ===========================================================================
# Spoof Detection - repository ignore rules
#
# Intentionally TRACKED (do not ignore):
#   - notebooks/                       Jupyter notebooks, canonical experiment record
#   - notes/                           user's personal notes (agents must not read)
#   - manifests/                       train_seed42.csv provenance manifest
#   - reports/                         experiment reports and small result tables
#   - Models/*/MODELS.md               model iteration documentation
#   - tests/test1/                     eight external smoke-test clips + results
#   - pyproject.toml, uv.lock          dependency source of truth
#   - .python-version                  pinned interpreter
#
# Intentionally IGNORED:
#   - Bibliography/                    user's papers (agents must not read)
#   - data/                            ~18 GB; re-download/regenerate (see AGENTS.md)
#   - model checkpoints (*.pth etc.)   never commit binaries (AGENTS.md G8)
#   - .venv/                           local environment, ~6 GB
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python build artifacts and caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
eggs/
.eggs/
sdist/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# Test / lint / type-check caches and coverage output
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pyre/
.hypothesis/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
nosetests.xml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtual environments and local secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/
env.bak/
venv.bak/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Jupyter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model checkpoints and other large binaries
#   Keep Models/<IterationN>/MODELS.md; ignore only the weights themselves.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.tflite
*.h5
*.hdf5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Datasets and generated data
#   Everything under data/ is reproducible from the ASVspoof 2019 LA download
#   plus scripts/reproduce_train_seed42.py. Never commit it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/data/
/archive.zip
ASVspoof2019*.zip
ASVspoof2019*.tar.gz

# E1.1 per-frontend render manifests: 18 CSVs, ~134 MB of per-image paths and
# SHA-256 values. Regenerate with `make e1-1-export`. The small provenance and
# parity summary is committed at reports/phase1/e1_1_frontend/export_manifest.json
# instead, and `manifests/train_seed42.csv` (the training membership record)
# stays tracked.
/manifests/e1_1_frontend/

# E1.2 per-condition render manifests (~8 conditions x 3 splits of image paths
# and SHA-256 values). Regenerate with `make e1-2-export`; the small provenance
# and parity summary is committed at
# reports/phase1/e1_2_rendering/export_manifest.json instead.
/manifests/e1_2_rendering/

# E1.2 per-clip score CSVs are regenerable and would add ~200-300 MB to the
# repository. Aggregate metrics, summaries and per-attack tables stay tracked.
/reports/phase1/e1_2_rendering/runs/**/scores_*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and temporary files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
*.temp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Others
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Papers and sources for the user. Not committed; agents must not read it
# (see AGENTS.md G1).
/Bibliography/
